<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Decimal currency jingle</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1966</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words, same tune</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Australian Folk Songs (Burl Ives)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1952</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Recording by A. L. Lloyd</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1956</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Recording by William Clauson</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1958</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Olivia Down Under (Olivia Newton-John)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1988</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in the television special</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The 1891 version, sung by Chloe and Jason Roweth for ABC TV</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2014</span><span class="sg-chain-h">revival of the first printed text</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ring the Bell, Watchman (Henry Clay Work)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune; first verse a parody of its words</span></li></ul></section>
